---
// Rebuilt in the homepage design system (home.css). Copy unchanged; values that
// feed a diagram live in src/data/diagnostic.json.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import HomeHeader from '../components/home/HomeHeader.astro';
import HomeFooter from '../components/home/HomeFooter.astro';
import HomeCta from '../components/home/HomeCta.astro';
import Lenses3D from '../components/art/Lenses3D.astro';
import diagnostic from '../data/diagnostic.json';
import timelines from '../data/timelines.json';
import fit from '../data/fit.json';

const { incentive, lenses, phases, needs, returns, weeks, findingPages } = diagnostic;
const set = fit.diagnostic;
const need = set.items.length - 1;

const heroPanel = [
  { label: 'Duration', value: '[PLACEHOLDER]' },
  { label: 'Fee', value: '[PLACEHOLDER]' },
  { label: 'Deliverable', value: 'A written finding' },
];
---

<Base
  title="A diagnostic of process, data and unit economics | KalTech"
  description="Every engagement begins with a diagnostic against process, data and unit economics. It ends in a written finding and a scope priced against it, for a fixed fee."
  breadcrumb={[{ name: 'Diagnostic', path: '/diagnostic' }]}
  chrome="own"
>
  <HomeHeader />

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="h-hero h-hero-sm h-dark" id="top" data-fx-hero>
    <div class="h-hero-bg" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="h-hero-grid"></span>
      <span class="h-orb h-orb-a"></span>
      <span class="h-orb h-orb-b"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="h-wrap h-hero-inner">
      <div class="h-hero-copy">
        <p class="h-badge m-reveal"><span class="h-badge-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>The diagnostic</p>
        <h1 class="h-h1 h-lines">
          <span class="h-line">Every engagement</span>
          <span class="h-line">begins with a</span>
          <span class="h-line"><em class="h-mark">diagnostic</em>.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="h-lead m-reveal">
          It runs against three lenses and ends in a written finding with a scope priced against it.
          Companies that proceed to a build do so with the constraint already established. Companies
          that do not proceed keep the finding.
        </p>
        <div class="h-actions m-reveal">
          <a class="h-btn h-btn-primary" href="/contact" data-magnetic>
            <span>Get an AI Strategy Consult</span><span class="h-btn-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <dl class="dg-facts m-reveal">
          {heroPanel.map((i) => (
            <div><dt class="sv-label">{i.label}</dt><dd>{i.value}</dd></div>
          ))}
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="h-hero-viz">
        <Lenses3D lenses={lenses.map((l) => l.label)} hot={diagnostic.gate.bindingIndex} label="Three lenses in a row with a beam passing through them; the beam turns at the binding lens." />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why it exists -->
  <section class="h-sec h-dark" id="why">
    <div class="h-dark-bg" aria-hidden="true"><span class="h-orb h-orb-c"></span></div>
    <div class="h-wrap dg-why">
      <div>
        <p class="h-eyebrow m-reveal">Why it exists</p>
        <h2 class="h-h2 m-reveal">A firm that builds should not be <span class="h-accent">trusted</span> to say what needs building.</h2>
        <p class="h-body dg-p m-reveal">
          That is the honest form of the objection, and we do not answer it by promising to be careful.
          We answer it by charging for the finding as a document rather than as the opening phase of a
          build, which means the diagnostic covers its own cost whatever it concludes. Where the work
          recommends less than the client came in asking for, or nothing at all, we have already been
          paid for the work that established it.
        </p>
        <p class="h-body dg-p m-reveal">
          The alternative arrangement, where the assessment is free and the revenue sits entirely in what
          follows, has one predictable output. Free assessments recommend builds. Not because the people
          writing them are dishonest, but because a firm that has absorbed the cost of the analysis has an
          interest in a particular conclusion, and interests are more reliable than intentions.
        </p>
        <p class="h-body dg-p m-reveal">
          The diagnostic fee is not credited against a subsequent build. Crediting it would reintroduce the
          incentive the fee exists to remove.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="dg-inct">
        <div class="dg-inct-row dg-inct-head m-reveal">
          <span></span><span class="sv-label">Free assessment</span><span class="sv-label">Paid finding</span>
        </div>
        {
          incentive.map((r) => (
            <div class="dg-inct-row m-reveal">
              <span class="dg-inct-key">{r.key}</span>
              <span class="dg-inct-free"><span class="dg-inct-cell">Free assessment</span>{r.free}{'bars' in r && r.bars && <span class="dg-bar"><span style={`width:${Math.round(r.bars.free * 100)}%`}></span></span>}</span>
              <span class="dg-inct-paid"><span class="dg-inct-cell">Paid finding</span>{r.paid}{'bars' in r && r.bars && <span class="dg-bar"><span style={`width:${Math.round(r.bars.paid * 100)}%`}></span></span>}</span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The three lenses -->
  <section class="h-sec h-bone" id="lenses">
    <div class="h-wrap">
      <div class="h-head">
        <div class="h-head-main">
          <h2 class="h-h2 m-reveal">Process, data, unit economics.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="h-sub m-reveal">
          One of the three is usually binding. The diagnostic establishes which, what it costs to leave in
          place, and what it would take to move. The three are examined in this order because a data problem
          examined before a process problem returns an answer that is technically correct and operationally
          useless.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="dg-lenses">
        {
          lenses.map((l, i) => (
            <article class={i === 0 ? 'dg-lens is-binding m-reveal' : 'dg-lens m-reveal'} data-spotlight>
              <div class="dg-lens-top">
                <p class="dg-lens-num">{l.num}</p>
                <p class="sv-label">{l.label}</p>
                <span class="dg-flag">{i === 0 ? diagnostic.gate.binding : diagnostic.gate.clear}</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="h-h3">{l.heading}</h3>
              <p class="h-body">{l.body}</p>
              <div class="dg-lens-aside">
                <p class="sv-label">What we examine</p>
                <p class="h-body">{l.examine}</p>
                <p class="sv-label">When this lens is binding</p>
                <p class="h-body">{l.binding}</p>
              </div>
              <p class="h-lens-ask"><strong>We ask:</strong> {l.ask}</p>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p class="sv-cap m-reveal">
        An illustration. Which lens is binding is what the diagnostic establishes, and it is not the same
        one twice running.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it runs -->
  <section class="h-sec h-white" id="runs">
    <div class="h-wrap">
      <div class="h-head">
        <div class="h-head-main">
          <p class="h-eyebrow m-reveal">How it runs</p>
          <h2 class="h-h2 m-reveal">What the {weeks} <span class="h-accent">weeks</span> actually consist of.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="h-sub m-reveal">
          The diagnostic is run by the engineers who would build against it, which is the reason it can be
          short. There is no discovery team assembling context for a delivery team that has not been hired
          yet, and no phase in which the work is explained a second time to the people who will actually do
          it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="sv-bar m-reveal" role="img" aria-label="Access and interviews, then evidence, the longest phase, then the finding.">
        {timelines.diagnosticPhases.map((s) => <span class="sv-seg sv-seg-solid" style={`flex:${s.width}`}></span>)}
      </div>
      <p class="sv-gate m-reveal"><span class="sv-gate-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>{weeks} weeks</p>

      <ol class="sv-steps dg-phases">
        {
          phases.map((ph) => (
            <li class="sv-step m-reveal" data-spotlight>
              <p class="sv-step-num">{ph.num}</p>
              <h3 class="h-h3">{ph.title}</h3>
              <p class="h-body">{ph.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <p class="sv-cap m-reveal">{timelines.caption}</p>

      <div class="dg-needs">
        <div>
          <p class="sv-label">What we need from you</p>
          <ul class="dg-needs-list">{needs.map((n) => <li class="h-body">{n}</li>)}</ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="sv-label">What we do not need</p>
          <p class="h-body">
            A brief, a requirements document, or a vendor evaluation. If one exists we will read it, but the
            diagnostic does not start from it, and where the finding disagrees with it we will say so.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What it returns -->
  <section class="h-sec h-bone" id="returns">
    <div class="h-wrap dg-returns">
      <div class="dg-ret-left">
        <h2 class="h-h2 m-reveal">What it <span class="h-accent">returns</span>.</h2>
        <div class="dg-facs m-reveal" aria-hidden="true">
          <p class="sv-label">KalTech Diagnostic Finding</p>
          <div class="dg-facs-lines">
            {
              returns.map((r) => (
                <p class="dg-facs-line">
                  <span class="dg-facs-num">{r.num}</span>
                  <span class="dg-facs-label">{r.short}</span>
                  <span class="dg-facs-lead"></span>
                  <span class="dg-facs-page">{r.page}</span>
                </p>
              ))
            }
          </div>
          <div class="dg-facs-greek"><i></i><i></i><i class="s"></i></div>
          <p class="sv-label">{findingPages} pages</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dg-ret-right">
        {
          returns.map((r) => (
            <div class="dg-ret m-reveal">
              <p class="dg-ret-num">{r.num}</p>
              <div>
                <p class="dg-ret-head">{r.head}</p>
                <p class="h-body">{r.body}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
        <p class="h-body dg-ret-note">
          The finding runs to roughly {findingPages} pages and is written to be read by someone who was not
          in the interviews. Clients take it to boards, to lenders and to their own technology teams, and it
          is written on the assumption that they will. Every figure in it is traceable to something we saw
          rather than something we were told, which is also why some of the numbers in it are smaller than
          the ones the business currently reports.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What it costs -->
  <section class="h-sec h-white" id="costs">
    <div class="h-wrap">
      <div class="h-head">
        <div class="h-head-main">
          <p class="h-eyebrow m-reveal">What it costs</p>
          <h2 class="h-h2 m-reveal">A <span class="h-accent">fixed fee</span>, agreed before the work starts.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="dg-cols">
        <div class="dg-big m-reveal">
          <p class="dg-big-fig">[PLACEHOLDER]</p>
          <p class="sv-label">Fixed fee, agreed in advance</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="h-body dg-p">
            Fixed at the outset and not adjusted by what the work finds, which means the fee is identical
            whether the finding recommends a build, a smaller build than the one you came in with, or no
            build at all.
          </p>
          <p class="h-body dg-p">
            The scope that follows is priced separately and by the team that would deliver it, so the
            estimate is written by the people who have to meet it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What it is not -->
  <section class="h-sec h-bone" id="isnot">
    <div class="h-wrap">
      <blockquote class="h-pull h-pull-light m-reveal">
        Sometimes the finding is that nothing should be built. We deliver that as readily as any other.
      </blockquote>
      <div class="dg-cols dg-cols-top">
        <div>
          <p class="sv-label">What it is not</p>
          <p class="h-body dg-p">This is not a sales document. We are not pitching you a service at the end of it.</p>
          <p class="h-body dg-p">
            Often the answer is that the thing you asked for should not be built, or that the real problem
            is somewhere else entirely. We tell you that plainly, in writing, and you keep the finding
            either way.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="dg-pair">
          <div class="dg-big m-reveal">
            <p class="dg-big-fig dg-big-sm">[PLACEHOLDER]</p>
            <p class="sv-label">Of the last [PLACEHOLDER] diagnostics recommended less than the client asked for</p>
          </div>
          <div class="dg-big m-reveal">
            <p class="dg-big-fig dg-big-sm">[PLACEHOLDER]</p>
            <p class="sv-label">Recommended nothing be built</p>
          </div>
          <p class="sv-cap">Figures cover [PLACEHOLDER].</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Useful when -->
  <section class="h-sec h-white" id="fit">
    <div class="h-wrap">
      <div class="sv-fit" data-fit data-fit-threshold={need}>
        <div class="sv-fit-main">
          <h2 class="h-h2" id="fit-diagnostic-title">{set.title}</h2>
          <ul class="sv-fit-list" aria-labelledby="fit-diagnostic-title">
            {
              set.items.map((text) => (
                <li class="sv-fit-row">
                  <label class="sv-fit-label">
                    <input class="sv-fit-box" type="checkbox" data-fit-box data-js-control />
                    <span class="h-body">{text}</span>
                  </label>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </div>
        <aside class="sv-fit-side" data-js-control>
          <p class="sv-fit-count" aria-live="polite"><span data-fit-n>0</span> of {set.items.length}</p>
          <p class="sv-fit-cta" data-fit-cta>
            <a class="h-btn h-btn-primary" href={fit.cta.href}><span>{fit.cta.label}</span><span class="h-btn-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <div class="sv-not">
        <h3 class="h-h3">{set.notTitle}</h3>
        <ul class="sv-not-list">{set.not.map((t) => <li class="h-body">{t}</li>)}</ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- A worked example -->
  <section class="h-sec h-dark" id="worked">
    <div class="h-dark-bg" aria-hidden="true"><span class="h-orb h-orb-c"></span></div>
    <div class="h-wrap">
      <div class="h-head">
        <div class="h-head-main">
          <p class="h-eyebrow m-reveal">A worked example</p>
          <h2 class="h-h2 m-reveal">What the finding <span class="h-accent">changed</span>.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="dg-cols dg-cols-top">
        <div>
          <p class="h-body dg-p">
            [PLACEHOLDER] came in asking for a scoring model to shorten lending decisions. The brief named
            the model, the vendor shortlist and the launch quarter.
          </p>
          <p class="h-body dg-p">The diagnostic ran all three lenses. The binding one was [PLACEHOLDER].</p>
          <p class="h-body dg-p">
            The finding said the brief as written addressed a symptom rather than the constraint, and set
            out what had to be settled before a model could return a result anyone could defend.
          </p>
          <p class="h-body dg-p">
            What was built was smaller than the brief. The system that removed the constraint came first,
            and the model followed once the inputs it depended on could be trusted.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="dg-delta m-reveal">
          <div class="dg-delta-row">
            <span class="sv-label">Scope requested &#183; [PLACEHOLDER]</span>
            <span class="dg-delta-bar"><i style="width:100%"></i></span>
          </div>
          <div class="dg-delta-row">
            <span class="sv-label">Scope delivered &#183; [PLACEHOLDER]</span>
            <span class="dg-delta-bar dg-delta-hot"><i style="width:46%"></i></span>
          </div>
          <p class="sv-cap">The difference is what the diagnostic found.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <HomeCta />
  <HomeFooter />
</Base>
